# Rows to merge into docs/TESTING.md

Source: Phase 2 (refactoring-patterns), first pass on `play/src/pusher/services/SocketManager.ts` (2026-11-12). Baseline `HEAD` = `08040b7e0`. Evidence: `docs/audits/tech-debt/phase2-socketmanager/README.md`. Line numbers marked "after" are in the file after all five patches.

## Test Strategy line (P1, replaces the SocketManager P1 bullet)

- **P1: the per-socket back stream handlers of `handleConnectToRoom` (after `SocketManager.ts:281-286` registers them; `handleMessageFromBack` `:322-366`, `closeSocketWhenBackEnds` `:368-401`, `closeSocketWhenBackFails` `:403-431`).** Every message from the back to one browser passes through `handleMessageFromBack`. The `end` and `error` handlers decide when the pusher closes the socket.

## Safety Net Map row (replaces the P1 row)

| Module | Pinned behaviors | Test files | Gaps |
|---|---|---|---|
| `SocketManager.ts`: connection to the back and relay (P1) | Each socket opens one back stream and writes `connectToRoomMessage`. One room stream per room URL, opened with `initRoomMessage`. `roomJoinedMessage` is relayed and subscribes the stored viewport's zones. Empty messages and `backConnectionCloseReasonMessage` are not relayed. The stream's `end` closes the socket with `WS_CLOSE_CODE_SESSION_DESTROYED` and `"Back lost: <reason>"`. The stream's `error` closes the socket with `WS_CLOSE_CODE_SESSION_DESTROYED` and `"Error while connecting to back server"`, ends the socket's back stream once, unsubscribes its zone, cancels the room stream and removes the room; a second `error` closes nothing more. Nothing is relayed after either. SM-02: a join confirmed after the pusher closed the socket takes no zone (flipped by `fix-SM-02.patch`; before it, the room outlived its last socket). | `play/tests/pusher/SocketManagerRoomTraffic.test.ts` | `handleJoinRoom`'s `joinRoomMessage` content; the `error` handler's log line and its own `catch`; the analytics session opened by a late join (SM-02, still open) |

## Characterization Backlog (replaces the item "`SocketManager` back stream `error` handler, and the analytics session...")

- [x] `SocketManager` back stream `error` handler: close code and reason, one cleanup, nothing relayed after it, a second `error` ignored (test "closes the socket once when its back stream fails, and relays nothing afterwards", `01-characterize-back-stream-error-handler.patch`; mutants E1, E2, E3 killed)
- [ ] `SocketManager` analytics session that a late join opens after `closeConnection` (SM-02 remainder; risk medium, P2)

## CI Gates

No change. The new test runs inside `npm test` with the rest of `SocketManagerRoomTraffic.test.ts`.
